# Hero Recruitment — Design Freeze

Source of truth: `GAME_LOGIC.md`. Tune example numbers in `src/shared/GameConfig.lua`. Do not break these rules.

## Economy

- Only Gold and Magic Stone.
- Heroes produce Magic Stone, never Gold.
- Converter is always `1 Magic Stone = 1 Gold`. Upgrade speed only.

## Recruitment

- Recruit Fee is paid to roll a candidate. **Accept is free.**
- High-tier (expensive) Heroes have a very low roll chance.
- Recruit Fee is never refunded, including on Reject or Sell.
- Max 10 pending cards on the Recruitment Board. Recruit 1X / 5X / 10X fill empty slots. Click an opened card to accept that one. TAKE ALL accepts all; CLEAR ALL rejects all.
- Candidate stats lock at generation. No reroll, expire, or mutate.

## Sell

- Catalog value by tier is locked at Accept as `AcceptCost` (not charged).
- Refund is `floor(AcceptCost * 0.25)` Gold. That 25% is the maximum.
- Seed / starter Heroes can be sold. Refund is `floor(AcceptCost * 0.25)` of the tier catalog locked at grant. `RAIDING` Heroes cannot be sold.
- Sell is not Combine. Implement in Phase 4 (`PHASES.md`).

## Display

- World display uses Workspace assets named `hero` inside the player's academy folder (`AKADEMI1`–`AKADEMI6`).
- Each player owns **one** academy. Max **6** players per server.
- Maximum **40** Heroes total. Recruit and Accept are blocked at 40/40 until a Hero is sold.
- Maximum **40** Heroes on pads (`ACTIVE`). If there are fewer pads, extras go to Bag (`BAGGED`) but still count toward the 40 cap.
- `ACTIVE` and `BAGGED` produce Magic Stone. `RAIDING` does not.

## Raid

- Team size is 1–5 heroes.
- Recommended Power is not a hard gate.
- Power at or above Recommended can shorten Raid time (floor 50% of map duration). Under-power keeps full time.
- Fail = no reward, no hero loss. `RAIDING` heroes pause production.

Studio AI should read `ReplicatedStorage.Shared.GameRules`.
